1. Difference between QA and QC

Quality Assurance (QA)
* Focuses on process
* Goal is to prevent defects
* Ensures the right process is followed to build quality software
* Activities: process definition, standards, audits, improvements
* Done by: QA team, Test Lead, Managers

Quality Control (QC)
* Focuses on product
* Goal is to find defects (bugs)
* Ensures the product meets requirements
* Activities: testing, defect identification, validation
* Done by: Testers, Developers

2. Explain in detail about STLC
1. Requirement Analysis: Tester studies requirements
Test Planning: Create Test Plan document
Test Case Development: Write Test cases, Test scenarios, Test data
Test Environment Setup: Prepare environment where we test the application
Test Execution: Execute test cases
Test Closure: Testing is completed and prepare Test Execution Report
